From 2befee5802d38ca10423aad8e80e5d1641216c77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cilium Authors <dev@cilium.io>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] tcp_proxy: Allow filters to wait for peer close

A protocol filter may need either side of a raw TCP proxy connection to remain
open after its local stream has ended so the peer can finish a protocol-level
close handshake. Add per-connection filter-state timeouts which make TCP proxy
flush pending writes and wait for the corresponding peer to close.

The raw TCP connection pool copies the upstream timeout into each TcpUpstream
when it is created, leaving the GenericUpstream extension interface unchanged.
The TCP proxy filter applies the downstream timeout when a raw TCP upstream
closes normally.

Data received from upstream during the final upstream drain interval cannot be
delivered to the closed downstream connection and is discarded. Preserve the
existing close behavior for connections which do not opt in, and always
propagate resets without delay.
